Dear Adam,

> I'm just surprised
> that commutativity doesn't hold.

A*B is is not the equivalent notation of any combination of A, B and
A:B. It is only the equivalent of A+B+A:B. When your design is
completely balanced, the output should be the same regardless of the
order. However, with unbalanced/incomplete designs you will get
different outputs. This is because of the famous Type I / Type III
sums of squares issue. To be honest I don't think this is the answer
to your problem, since repeated-measures designs require only 1 data
point per cell. Is any data point missing?

Francisco

